0,Matbat language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matbat_language,"Matbat is a heavily Papuan -influenced Austronesian language spoken in Southwest Papua, Indonesia, on the island of Misool, Raja Ampat Islands. [1] Its dialects are Magey and Tomolol. [2]: 17 Similar to the neighboring Ma'ya language, Matbat is one of a handful of Austronesian languages with true lexical tone rather than a pitch-accent system or complete lack of phonemic tonal contrasts as ...",Matbat,Austronesian
